[0.000, "o", "ent behavioral fixture evidence and its limitations.\r\n+\r\n+## Behavioral result\r\n+\r\n+An independent Codex agent followed the installed skill on synthetic metadata in isolated directories, using scripts to materialize its decisions. Ten observable artifact checks passed and zero failed: eligible coverage (including squash merge), category assignment, exclusions, duplicate removal, absence of source internal details, preservation of prior notes, rerun without duplicates, missing-evidence non-mutation with draft/request, and an explicit all-excluded result. The rerun was an inspection resulting in no destination write. See `trial/report.md` and `trial/checks.json` for scope and artifacts.\r\n+\r\n+Status: validated for these fixture behaviors and the alternative structural checks. The pinned Python validator, live git/forge retrieval, default date resolution, and actual automatic discovery remain unverified. No comparative benchmark, human preference approval, timing, or token telemetry is claimed.\r\n"]
